course: dictionary
lesson: 14272
title: Words about night animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nocturnally is an adverb. It tells you when or how something happens. It means at night, or during the night. We use it most for animals that are awake and busy after dark.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «Owls hunt nocturnally, flying quietly over the fields.» The words hunt, flying and quietly show the owl is active, and the rest of the sentence tells you it does this at night.
explain: Nocturnally has a partner word, diurnally, which means in the day. Animals that sleep at night and play in the sun are diurnal. When you find a tricky word, ask: is it the same as this, or the opposite?
fact: Nocturnally means at night, especially for animals that are active during the night.
fact: Owls, bats, hedgehogs, foxes and badgers are nocturnal animals, so they are active nocturnally.
fact: Nocturnal animals usually sleep during the day.
fact: The opposite of nocturnally is diurnally, which means in the day.
fact: «Bats feed nocturnally, catching moths in the dark.»
exercise: «Owls hunt nocturnally, so you will see them mostly after dark.» What does nocturnally mean? | *At night | Under water | Very loudly | In the morning
exercise: Which word means the opposite of nocturnally? | sleepily | nightly | nocturnal | *diurnally
exercise: «Badgers come out nocturnally to dig for worms.» Find the word that tells you when the badgers are active. | *nocturnally | dig | worms | badgers
test: Which animal is nocturnal and sleeps in the day? | *Bat | Daisy | Robin | Butterfly
test: «Moths fly nocturnally around the lamp.» What does nocturnally mean here? | Under the ground | In the day | *At night | Very brightly
exam: Which sentence uses nocturnally correctly? | Owls fly nocturnally at noon. | *Hedgehogs feed nocturnally, snuffling for beetles after dark. | Foxes sleep nocturnally in the morning sun. | Hedgehogs feed nocturnally at lunchtime, in the sunshine.
